    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0437" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v02/pg407"/>

                <head>221. Telegram From the Mission at the United
                        Nations to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d221-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-10-07T20:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                                1960—8 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>926. U.S. initiative re Soviet actions in GA
                        (Tosec 49).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d221-f2"
                    /></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>In my opinion Khrushchev has
                        overplayed his hand with neutralists and others here both through his bitter
                        attacks against U.S., through his attacks on SYG, and his personal behavior in plenary hall when Macmillan spoke.<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d221-f3"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>There is prevailing sentiment in GA against
                        cold-war atmosphere and Soviets are suffering for having made such attacks
                        basis their posture in GA.</item>
                    <pb facs="0438" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In these circumstances I do not think we should submit item of nature
                        contained reftel. We will have ample
                        opportunity in rebuttal to Soviet items and charges to include in speeches
                        and possibly even resolutions main elements contained in draft memorandum of
                        explanation. I believe this is way in which we will be most effective this
                        year.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Wadsworth</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
